# HUMMUS FATTEH
## info  
* About 30 minutes prep, 1 hour total
* about 4 servings  

## ingredients
* 2 cups cooked chickpeas, divided
* 1/3 cup tahini
* 1/4 cup fresh lemon juice
* 2 cloves garlic, minced
* 1/2 teaspoon ground cumin
* 1/2 teaspoon salt, plus more to taste
* 1/3 cup olive oil, divided
* 4 pita rounds, cut into wedges
* 8 ounces ground beef or lamb
* 1 small onion, finely chopped
* 1 teaspoon ground cumin
* 1/2 teaspoon ground cinnamon
* 1/4 cup pine nuts
* 1/4 cup chopped fresh parsley
* 1/4 cup plain yogurt (optional)
* Paprika or Aleppo pepper for garnish

## steps  
1. Preheat the oven to 375°F. Toss pita wedges with 2 tablespoons of olive oil and salt, then spread on a baking sheet and bake until crisp and golden, about 10 minutes.
1. Heat 1 tablespoon of olive oil in a skillet over medium heat. Add chopped onion and cook until softened.
1. Add ground beef or lamb, cumin, cinnamon, and a pinch of salt. Cook, breaking up the meat, until browned and cooked through. Set aside.
1. In a blender or food processor, combine 1 1/2 cups cooked chickpeas, tahini, lemon juice, garlic, cumin, salt, and remaining olive oil. Blend until smooth, adding a little water if needed to reach a creamy consistency.
1. In a small skillet, toast pine nuts over medium heat until lightly browned. Remove and set aside.
1. Arrange toasted pita chips in a shallow serving dish. Spread the hummus on top of the pita, leaving some chips visible.
1. Scatter the remaining chickpeas and cooked meat over the hummus.
1. Drizzle with yogurt if using, sprinkle with toasted pine nuts, chopped parsley, and a dusting of paprika or Aleppo pepper.

## notes  
* For extra richness, warm the hummus slightly before assembling.
* You can swap the ground meat for toasted pine nuts alone for a vegetarian version.

